{
  "_about": "Raids: the defense of the village on the map, in light real time (src/core/world/raids.js and src/core/world/systems/raid.js). Places are in map cells [x, y]; lengths are in half blocks (one cell is 2) and times in seconds. sling: the slingshot (the angle in radians; max: the longest pull, as a count of half blocks; the stone lands exactly at the count; hit: how near an enemy must be to the landing point). posts: the distance posts along the road from the wall. grades: the level of the raids (1, 2, or 3) for the grade that the player gave; at level 1 a lost raid takes nothing. gateBar: the seconds that the bar stays down (hold), and the rest before the next tap. helperLooks: the looks of the villagers at the spots. companions: the look of a companion at the side of the hero. toolLines: the line that the elder or the smith says the first time that a tool comes (the flag raid.tool.<tool> keeps it). skills: the skill of each kind of commit (shot: the first shot at an enemy, by level; correct: the next shot after a miss at the same enemy). enemies: speed (half blocks each second: they walk, never run), hits (the hits before the enemy retreats), trap (the seconds on a trap; 0: the enemy breaks the trap), torch (range from the gate, tell, every, fly), sword (reach, tell, every), shield (the seconds of the wet shield after fire), boss (it does not retreat; it stands stunned for the next phase), calm (a creature that becomes calm). raids: tools (the tools of the raid, one more each raid: sling, gate, traps, helpers, nghe, water, fire, lightning, bamboo; a tool that is not in the raid is not on the map), trapPost and trapAsk (the post where a villager asks for a trap, in half blocks from the wall, and who asks; a trap put there is the skill event), ball (what the slingshot throws, when it is not a stone), wall (where the hero stands with the slingshot; the posts count from here), gate (where the enemies stop), dir (the road from the wall out), bar (the gate has a bar), waves (at: seconds after the start of the phase, kind, from, side: half blocks to the side), phases (the boss), pile and traps (the bamboo traps by the gate), road (the part of the road for traps, from and to along the road), spots and helpers (the villagers that the child can call), sources (the elements to drag: water, fire, lightning), allow (the losses that still win), take (what an enemy at the gate takes), introKey (the line before the raid), pauseKey (the line of the map in a raid: the map only pauses), mark and noteKey (a short, fair note after a win, with the seal Legend or History), historyKey (a fact of history after the note, with its own History seal), loot (the sacks of rice of a win: the child shares them behind the wall with Nghé and Gióng, the task share in data/trials.json), win (flags, gifts, and talks after a win), repeat (the raid can come again). steed: the companion rides his iron horse; the height of the seat in blocks (the same as STEED_SEAT in src/world/figures.js). The companion stands beside the road, away from the sources, the flags, and the pile (companionSpot in src/core/world/systems/raid.js).",
